. Defects in this gene have been associated with autosomal recessive spastic paraplegia-74 and with multiple mitochondrial dysfunctions syndrome-3. Two transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. The smaller isoform is not likely to be localized to the mitochondrion since it lacks the amino-terminal transit peptide. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2015].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q5T440","text":"Mitochondrial protein involved in the maturation of mitochondrial [4Fe-4S]-proteins in the late stage of the iron-sulfur cluster assembly pathway (PubMed:22323289, PubMed:23462291). Operates in cooperation with ISCA2 in the maturation of [4Fe-4S] proteins (PubMed:30269484). Involved in the maturation of mitochondrial 2Fe-2S proteins in the late stage of the iron-sulfur cluster assembly pathway."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}